  "body": "Fix: #5755\r\n\r\nThe schema registry's DuckDB projector crashes on the first checkpoint record it receives, usually shortly after startup, and doesn't restart, so schema queries stop seeing new or changed schemas.\r\n\r\n## Background\r\n\r\nThe projector keeps its read position in DuckDB, next to the data it writes. It reads with auto-commit off and runs its own position tracker, which it feeds every record it receives. That includes checkpoint records, which the subscription sends every so many events it reads and when it catches up to the end of the log. The tracker uses each record's sequence id to work out which positions are safe to save, and it rejects a record without one.\r\n\r\nWhile fixing the connectors controller overflow, #5739 assumed nothing tracks checkpoint records when auto-commit is off and stopped giving them a sequence id, so the first one that reaches the projector crashes it.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- **Checkpoint records are always numbered.**\r\n- **With auto-commit off, `Track` and `Commit` now track checkpoint records.** The consumer doesn't track them itself in that mode, so a numbered checkpoint that nobody tracks would leave a gap and stall commits.\r\n- **Events skipped by a JsonPath filter no longer overwrite `lastReadRecord`.** The caught-up record copies its sequence id, so it could pick up an empty one the same way.",
